 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Tobias \"upgraded\" Grandma Ilse's milking stool. Four legs. Cupholder. Heated seat.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 5.123
  },
  {
   "text": "If the milk wasn't ready by six, the cheese truck left without it.",
   "s": 5.323,
   "e": 8.273
  },
  {
   "text": "Grandma's old stool had three legs, a crack, and a name: Gerald.",
   "s": 8.473,
   "e": 11.691
  },
  {
   "text": "Tobias sat on the deluxe stool. It rocked. Clack. Clack. Clack.",
   "s": 11.891,
   "e": 14.979
  },
  {
   "text": "Daisy the cow got seasick watching and knocked the bucket over with her tail.",
   "s": 15.179,
   "e": 18.905
  },
  {
   "text": "So Tobias upgraded again: six legs. It rocked twice as much, like a table at a cheap cafe.",
   "s": 19.105,
   "e": 24.541
  },
  {
   "text": "Then ten legs: the Centipede Deluxe. It wobbled so hard it walked across the barn by itself.",
   "s": 24.741,
   "e": 30.053
  },
  {
   "text": "His fix: folded cardboard under one leg. Then two. Then he ran out and used Grandma's best cheese.",
   "s": 30.253,
   "e": 35.777
  },
  {
   "text": "At 5:58, the cheese truck honked, and Tobias had milked exactly one cup. Into the cupholder.",
   "s": 35.977,
   "e": 41.036
  },
  {
   "text": "So why does a three-legged stool never rock?",
   "s": 41.236,
   "e": 43.311
  },
  {
   "text": "Three feet always touch the ground, any ground, like a camera tripod on a rocky beach.",
   "s": 43.611,
   "e": 48.226
  },
  {
   "text": "On a bumpy floor, a fourth leg always hangs in the air. Sit down, and you rock onto it. Clack.",
   "s": 48.426,
   "e": 53.558
  },
  {
   "text": "Grandma sat on Gerald. Not one wobble. Full bucket in four minutes.",
   "s": 53.958,
   "e": 57.614
  },
  {
   "text": "Tobias still uses the Centipede Deluxe. As a coat rack. It wobbles.",
   "s": 57.814,
   "e": 61.942
  }
 ],
